---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="XRP NO BALL GAMES | XRP KIDs Timeline, Canon Cards &amp; Verification Rules"
  description="Expanded XRP NO BALL GAMES hub with canon timeline, character cards, 100/89/11 framing, proof requirements and hard verify-before-interaction disclaimers."
  current="xrp"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">XRP NO BALL GAMES</span>
    <h1>Where the sign hits the ledger.</h1>
    <p>
      This is the XRPL-side NO BALL GAMES branch. It combines internal canon lore with strict public claim discipline. Lore stays lore. Chain facts need proof.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section split-grid">
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Public framing</span>
      <h2>Internal canon + verification guardrails.</h2>
      <p>
        XRP KIDs, Alpha Aaron, FRET, $PMSL and Block Buster OG are presented as NO BALL GAMES internal canon and project structure unless official issuer and marketplace records are attached.
      </p>
      <p>
        This approach protects collectors, preserves tone and avoids fake certainty.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Hard disclaimer</span>
      <h2>Verify issuer. Verify collection.</h2>
      <p>
        Any token or NFT reference must be independently verified through official issuer details, collection records and XRPL ledger sources before interaction. Nothing on this page is financial advice.
      </p>
      <div class="coming-soon-tag">Nothing here is financial advice</div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Canon timeline</h2>
      <p>Locked internal timeline points for the XRP branch.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="timeline">
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2025</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>Genesis launch concept</h3>
          <p>100 XRP KIDs form the internal genesis set and establish the branch identity.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2028</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>Alpha signal appears</h3>
          <p>Alpha Aaron enters as the machine-control antagonist arc in canon.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2028–2029</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>Capture phase</h3>
          <p>89 of the 100 KIDs are captured in canon, shifting the story into a resistance war.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2029+</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>FRET and $PMSL fork shield</h3>
          <p>The remaining 11 free KIDs become the resistance heart around FRET and the $PMSL hard-fork shield concept.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2030–2032</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>Block Buster OG emerges</h3>
          <p>The hidden 1/1 intervention layer appears through the Fibonacci-era lore arc.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="timeline-item">
        <strong>2035</strong>
        <div>
          <h3>New Dawn</h3>
          <p>Signs become doors. The 11 free KIDs remain symbolic survivors while Alpha's threat persists at low signal.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Character and system cards</h2>
      <p>Core lore entities used across the XRP pages.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">XRP KIDs</span>
        <h3>Genesis collectible core</h3>
        <p>The branch starts with a 100-piece canonical set tied to humour, rebellion and play under pressure.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Alpha Aaron</span>
        <h3>Capture antagonist</h3>
        <p>Represents centralising machine logic that buys culture and tries to lock it down.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">FRET</span>
        <h3>Fresh Rapid Elite Team</h3>
        <p>Barbican-rooted resistance network of artists, coders, collectors and street-level signal runners.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">$PMSL</span>
        <h3>Hard-fork shield</h3>
        <p>Lore token concept around the 11 free KIDs; not a public token claim without issuer verification.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Block Buster OG</span>
        <h3>Hidden 1/1 archive key</h3>
        <p>Mythic intervention node carrying memory and anti-control logic through late-canon events.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section split-grid">
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Canonical count lock</span>
      <h2>100 / 89 / 11</h2>
      <ul class="list-clean">
        <li><strong>100 genesis KIDs</strong> are the origin set.</li>
        <li><strong>89 captured</strong> marks Alpha Aaron's domination phase.</li>
        <li><strong>11 free</strong> anchors the FRET/$PMSL resistance arc.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These numbers are lore canon here unless independently confirmed by records.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">What needs proof first</span>
      <h2>Before public token claims.</h2>
      <ul class="list-clean">
        <li>Issuer address and network confirmation.</li>
        <li>Verified collection records and marketplace pages.</li>
        <li>Token supply and trust-line data from official sources.</li>
        <li>Transaction/sales records from verifiable ledgers.</li>
        <li>Official project links for any interaction route.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-block">
    <div class="cta-block-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Need source depth?</span>
      <h2>Read the truth baselines before action.</h2>
      <p>Use research for full canon notes and source-needed details, then use contact for collector/lore/source enquiries.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}research/`}>Open research index</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}contact/`}>Submit enquiry</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
